 "result": "Look at `locate_main_app` in `src/tessel/cli.py:41-92`, specifically the factory branch at lines 66-92.\n\n**Why:**\n- Auto-discovery only tries `app`/`application`, then a lone `Tessel` instance, then the factories `create_app`/`make_app`. A factory is invoked with **no arguments** (`app_factory()`, line 72).\n- Your `create_app(config_name)` has a required argument, so that call raises `TypeError`.\n- `_bad_factory_args` (line 94) walks the traceback to see whether the error happened *before* entering the factory (a bad call signature, so it returns `True`) or inside it. For your factory it returns `True`, so `locate_main_app` raises `NoAppException` (\"Detected factory ... could not call it without arguments\") instead of using it.\n\n**Fix:** you don't need to change the code. Use the explicit form handled by `find_app_by_string` (line 120), which parses a function call expression:\n\n```\ntessel run --app 'yourmodule:create_app(\"production\")'\n```\n\nAlternatively, give `config_name` a default value, or expose a module-level `app = create_app(...)`.",
